From: Eric Berquist <eric.berquist@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] python313Packages.aio-pika: fix version metadata

aio-pika does not build: the 9.6.2 tag's pyproject.toml still declares
9.6.0, so the wheel's METADATA disagrees with the derivation and
pythonMetadataCheckPhase refuses it.

    The 'aio-pika' derivation has version '9.6.2' but .dist-info/METADATA
    specifies version '9.6.0'.

Upstream stopped bumping the version file after 9.6.0: both the 9.6.1
and 9.6.2 tags still carry `version = "9.6.0"`. The tags themselves are
real and distinct, so the version here is right and only the metadata is
wrong -- pyprojectVersionPatchHook rewrites it, as the error message
itself recommends.

This is the same slip as in aiormq, by the same upstream author, tagged
on the same day.

---
diff --git a/pkgs/development/python-modules/aio-pika/default.nix b/pkgs/development/python-modules/aio-pika/default.nix
index c795828..f9bd5c5 100644
--- a/pkgs/development/python-modules/aio-pika/default.nix
+++ b/pkgs/development/python-modules/aio-pika/default.nix
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
   aiormq,
   buildPythonPackage,
   fetchFromGitHub,
+  pyprojectVersionPatchHook,
   uv-build,
   yarl,
 }:
@@ -24,7 +25,10 @@ buildPythonPackage rec {
       --replace-fail "uv_build>=0.9.26,<0.10.0" uv_build
   '';
 
-  build-system = [ uv-build ];
+  build-system = [
+    pyprojectVersionPatchHook
+    uv-build
+  ];
 
   dependencies = [
     aiormq
